            <ArticleTitle>[Biological diagnosis in allergy and immunology].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>346-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diagnosis in allergy-immunology is based on clinical elements (History--Skin tests) and biological elements: search for IgE to allergens or for allergens that are presumed to be responsible and in the case of asthma or rhinitis on tests of respiratory function and/or rhinomanometry and/or nasofibroscopy; finally on provocation tests if necessary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
